# The port menu from the main menu: F1 opens it and says the opening, every
# category with its first row, entered with Right and left with Escape, a
# setting stepped both ways, a slider moved, the input device stepped to
# Keyboard and back, Restore defaults saying its status line, the lines
# between the rows read on Controls and Online, typing in a text field with
# a refused character, Escape on Resume closing it with "Back to game", then
# the gamepad's Back opening it again on the category used last, the
# shoulder and the D-pad moving and B going back a level and closing it.
# Waits on each announcement, so a missing or changed line fails the run.
# Run with accessibility on but muted, which the line reading needs (as
# run_level.py runs it):
#   python tools/a11y/drive.py --muted tools/a11y/port_menu.drive
# then grep -c -E '"(Saved|Settings save automatically|\w+ settings\.")'
# build/drive/last.log prints 0: the status line's "Saved." after every
# change, its first text and each focus's description are never spoken, a
# line too many that drive.py cannot fail on and run_level.py checks itself.
# The run's settings folder starts from the defaults, so Player name holds
# PLAYER and the connect code is the run's own. Display mode is never
# pressed or stepped: fullscreen would take the screen (drive.py refuses it).
# The update check is left out: Check now asks the network, and its result
# is written only at the next saved change or opening. Quit game is left out
# too, as it ends the run.

# Title screen to the main menu (main_menu.drive).
wait "state 0 scene 0$"
press Start until "boot scene: game mode"
press A until "boot scene: state 0 scene 1$" 20 0.3
sleep 1

# F1 opens the menu on Graphics, a fresh run's first category.
key F1
wait '"PC settings\. Graphics\. Up and down to choose, right to enter"$'

# Into the rows. Vertical sync off and on: the new value alone, "Saved."
# unsaid.
key Right
wait '"Display mode, Windowed, Left and right to change"$'
key Down
wait '"Vertical sync, On, Left and right to change"$'
key Right
wait '"Off"$'
key Left
wait '"On"$'
key Escape
wait '"Graphics"$'

# Audio: Master volume, a slider, a step down and back up.
key Down
wait '"Audio"$'
key Right
wait '"Master volume, slider, 100%\. Left and right to adjust\. Left/right or drag to adjust\."$'
key Left
wait '"95%"$'
key Right
wait '"100%"$'
key Down
wait '"Music volume, slider, 100%\. Left and right to adjust\. Background music volume\."$'
key Escape
wait '"Audio"$'

key Down
wait '"Gameplay"$'
key Right
wait '"Unlock everything, \w+, Left and right to change\. Unlock all 26 characters, 11 secret stages, and All-Star mode\."$'
key Escape
wait '"Gameplay"$'

# Controls: the input device stepped to Keyboard, with its live line, and
# back to Port 1.
key Down
wait '"Controls"$'
key Right
wait '"Input device, Port 1, Left and right to change\. No controller in this port\. Choose a controller port or Keyboard\. Select a row to change its binding\."$'
key Left
wait '"Keyboard, Player 1, Escape cancels, Delete clears a binding"$'
key Down
wait '"A, X, Enter to change"$'
key Up
wait '"Input device, Keyboard, Left and right to change\. '
key Right
wait '"Port 1, No controller in this port\."$'

# Down over the bindings, the heading between them, Restore defaults,
# pressed for its status line, and Menu button, then the keyboard's lines
# and Resume; Up from Resume is the sidebar's.
key Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Down
wait ', Enter to change"$'
key Down
wait '"Sticks and triggers"$'
key Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Down
wait '"Restore defaults: Restore, button\. Put this port back on its default mapping\."$'
key Return
wait '"Defaults restored\."$'
key Down
wait '"Menu button, back, Enter to change\. Choose the button that opens settings on all controllers\. Guide and F1 always work too\."$'
key Down
wait '"Keyboard"$'
key Down
wait '"WASD, arrows Move"$'
key Down Down Down Down Down Down Down
wait '"IJKL C-stick"$'
key Up
wait '"Enter Start"$'
key Down Down
wait '"Resume, button\. Close settings and return to the game\."$'
key Up
wait '"Accessibility"$'
key Up
wait '"Online"$'

# Online: Player name, typed into with the cursor at the field's start. #
# is refused, letters go in as capitals, and a full field says so;
# Backspace puts PLAYER back.
key Right
wait '"Player name, edit, PLAYER\. 1.8 letters or digits\. Changes apply to the next search\."$'
type "#ab1"
wait '"# not allowed"$'
wait '"APLAYER"$'
wait '"ABPLAYER"$'
wait '"Full, 8 characters at most"$'
key Backspace
wait '"APLAYER"$'
key Backspace
wait '"PLAYER"$'

# The lines between Online's rows, read in their turn, to Resume.
key Down
wait '"Your connect code, PLAYER#\w+"$'
key Down
wait "\"Friend's connect code, edit, blank\. Leave blank to host your code\. Open Online, Direct Connect in-game\.\"$"
key Down
wait '"Input delay, Auto, Left and right to change\. Automatic adapts to your connection\. Changes apply next match\."$'
key Down
wait '"Internet discovery can take a few minutes\. Some home networks cannot connect without a relay\."$'
key Down
wait '"Resume, button\. Close settings and return to the game\."$'

# Escape on Resume closes the menu, and the game runs again.
key Escape
wait '"Back to game"$'
press Down
wait '"VS\. Mode\. Multiplayer battles!"$'

# The gamepad's Back opens it on the category used last; the shoulder
# changes category, the D-pad enters the rows, and B goes back, then closes.
gamepad back
wait '"PC settings\. Online\. Up and down to choose, right to enter"$'
gamepad leftshoulder
wait '"Controls"$'
gamepad dpright
wait '"Input device, Port 1, Left and right to change\. '
gamepad b
wait '"Controls"$'
gamepad b
wait '"Back to game"$'
press Down
wait '"Trophies\. View trophies\."$'
